How about normally the henchman just follows you around.  If you want him/her
to do something, you #chat with him, and you get a menu:

What do you want your henchman to do?
a) Map (10 zorkmids)
b) Fight (100 zorkmids)
c) Sell you an item               [130% or so of shop price]
d) Pick up an item
e) Swap places with you
f) Try a magic item (100 zorkmids)

and any others I can't think of right now.
Mapping would involve giving him a direction and he goes that way as far as he can, randomly turning at intersections, etc.

Fighting: you designate a monster (with hjkl. commands) and he goes to fight it until he is at 20% or so hp, then he runs away

Sell you an item:  If he picks up an item you want, you can buy it from him at a premium price (it is his property, not exactly like a shopkeeper's stock).

The henchman could move like a unicorn, never moving next to a monster, never getting in direct line with one unless trapped (he can't teleport like a unicorn). You, however, can get next to him, and you need to to #chat with him.

Don't flame me over the numbers.  They're all relative, I just picked them out of a hat.  I do accept responsibility for the basic ideas though, and the numbers
are a ballpark estimate.
The list of actions could probably be extended (just now I think of
g) go somewhere [indicated w/ hjkl., and then resume normal motion.]

This would make him a convenience, but a certain drain on your gold and possibly items laying around in the dungeon (he won't make a beeline for them, but if he does step on one, give him a (random, about 40%) chance of picking it up.)


